This is a re-implementation of the classic macro processor GPM
with some minor extensions. The original implementation is
described in the article Strachey, Christopher (October 1965).
"A General Purpose  Macrogenerator". Computer Journal 8 (3): 225–241.
http://comjnl.oxfordjournals.org/content/8/3/225.full.pdf

This implementation is still a work in progress. It has
a few known bugs and a long list of proposed improvements.
The latest version of ggpm can be obtained by:
git clone https://sphinx.pinastri@code.google.com/p/ggpm/
 
Any contributions to the project are always welcome.
Please direct your questions, comments or patches to:

Peter Cherepanov <sphinx.pinastri@gmail.com>
Elina Batyrova   <lundrleht@gmail.com>

